1
00:00:58,937 --> 00:00:59,770
Amur.

2
00:01:01,625 --> 00:01:02,796
Amur.

3
00:01:07,353 --> 00:01:08,233
Hey.

4
00:01:11,770 --> 00:01:12,562
Amur.

5
00:01:13,238 --> 00:01:14,217
Amur.

6
00:01:27,593 --> 00:01:28,500
Amur.

7
00:01:28,697 --> 00:01:30,572
Ha ha ha ha.

8
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:35,875
Oh, I just knew you'd be by the lake again.

9
00:01:35,875 --> 00:01:36,541
Hey.

10
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:37,625
This month's meat,

11
00:01:37,625 --> 00:01:39,750
vegetables and daily supplies
are all on the counter.

12
00:01:39,750 --> 00:01:40,541
Mm.

13
00:01:41,166 --> 00:01:42,958
Alright, Mongke.

14
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:44,166
Put it on my tab.

15
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:46,031
Hey.

16
00:01:46,666 --> 00:01:49,375
Your tab, y'know...
it's been over half a year.

17
00:01:50,958 --> 00:01:52,250
How's business lately?

18
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,791
Why don't you settle up last quarter first?

19
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:56,562
Business?

20
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:58,500
Same as always.

21
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,101
Hit or miss.

22
00:02:01,155 --> 00:02:03,183
Hey, if business ain't good, get out there.

23
00:02:03,208 --> 00:02:04,585
Hand out some flyers, y'know.

24
00:02:04,938 --> 00:02:05,992
Oh right.

25
00:02:06,812 --> 00:02:07,906
Where's Xiaohei?

26
00:02:08,289 --> 00:02:09,844
How come he's not back yet?

27
00:02:10,875 --> 00:02:12,625
I can't hear him barking.

28
00:02:12,906 --> 00:02:14,322
Feels kinda strange.

29
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:19,083
Xiaohei...

30
00:02:20,422 --> 00:02:21,838
don't know where he went.

31
00:02:23,145 --> 00:02:24,645
Went out looking but couldn't find him.

32
00:02:26,601 --> 00:02:27,684
Let's wait a bit more.

33
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:31,070
Maybe if we wait,
he'll come back on his own.

34
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:34,541
Without Xiaohei to help out,

35
00:02:34,566 --> 00:02:36,608
it's really been a lot of trouble, y'know.

36
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:38,383
Before, whenever you ordered stuff,

37
00:02:38,579 --> 00:02:40,829
Xiaohei would carry it over himself.

38
00:02:41,583 --> 00:02:42,416
Hey.

39
00:02:43,507 --> 00:02:46,548
You don't think Xiaohei got eaten
by wolves on the way?

40
00:02:46,581 --> 00:02:47,623
Oh, go on, get outta here.

41
00:02:48,077 --> 00:02:49,710
You're the one who'd get eaten by wolves.

42
00:02:50,208 --> 00:02:51,601
Hey, it's getting dark, head home.

43
00:02:51,626 --> 00:02:52,914
Any later and there really might be wolves.

44
00:02:54,625 --> 00:02:56,000
I ain't scared of no wolves.

45
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,554
You study hard now.

46
00:02:58,958 --> 00:03:00,164
Do well on your exam.

47
00:03:01,156 --> 00:03:02,851
You're so long-winded.

48
00:03:03,015 --> 00:03:03,916
I'm already studying, aren't I?

49
00:03:03,916 --> 00:03:05,375
Yeah yeah, alright alright.

50
00:03:05,416 --> 00:03:06,734
I'm off, I'm off.

51
00:03:42,447 --> 00:03:43,572
Let's go, Xiaohei.

52
00:03:45,791 --> 00:03:46,666
Woof woof.

53
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:49,062
Xiaohei's hungry?

54
00:03:49,668 --> 00:03:51,273
Woof woof woof woof woof woof woof woof.

55
00:03:52,041 --> 00:03:53,267
Xiaohei's really hungry?

56
00:03:53,955 --> 00:03:55,414
Woof woof woof woof woof.

57
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:57,916
Then let's get you something tasty?

58
00:03:57,957 --> 00:03:58,749
Woof woof woof.

59
00:03:59,416 --> 00:04:00,208
Come on!

60
00:04:13,124 --> 00:04:15,509
I'm from Singapore.

61
00:04:16,957 --> 00:04:18,939
Before my father passed, he said

62
00:04:19,958 --> 00:04:23,041
"A person should see the great grasslands"

63
00:04:24,353 --> 00:04:25,666
That way, when you go,

64
00:04:26,023 --> 00:04:27,606
you won't have any regrets.

65
00:04:29,177 --> 00:04:32,510
I came to the grasslands
with my own willfulness.

66
00:04:33,958 --> 00:04:35,291
I never expected

67
00:04:35,874 --> 00:04:38,033
to encounter a pack of wolves.

68
00:04:39,255 --> 00:04:40,463
Fortunately,

69
00:04:41,223 --> 00:04:43,056
a black dog saved me

70
00:04:43,541 --> 00:04:44,875
and brought me here.

71
00:04:44,875 --> 00:04:45,458
Hey.

72
00:04:45,458 --> 00:04:46,791
Where I met him.

73
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:52,583
Hey.

74
00:04:54,395 --> 00:04:55,437
Who are you?

75
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:56,087
Hey.

76
00:04:56,112 --> 00:04:57,236
What happened to you?

77
00:06:24,012 --> 00:06:25,153
You're...

78
00:06:26,072 --> 00:06:26,906
Ah.

79
00:06:27,270 --> 00:06:28,489
You're awake.

80
00:06:28,879 --> 00:06:30,489
Here, let me take a look.

81
00:06:32,716 --> 00:06:34,034
(Symptoms in the Pharmacy: A Guide to
the Management of Common Illnesses)

82
00:06:34,059 --> 00:06:35,041
I'm a doctor.

83
00:06:35,227 --> 00:06:36,768
Stay still, don't move.

84
00:06:43,971 --> 00:06:45,180
The low fever has passed.

85
00:06:51,098 --> 00:06:52,181
Hungry?

86
00:06:52,206 --> 00:06:54,040
Here, let me get you a bowl of meat.

87
00:07:00,181 --> 00:07:01,239
Um...

88
00:07:02,098 --> 00:07:03,340
Where are my clothes?

89
00:07:03,875 --> 00:07:06,333
You were soaking wet when you arrived.

90
00:07:06,358 --> 00:07:08,090
I washed them and hung them out to dry.

91
00:07:09,122 --> 00:07:11,262
So I'm naked?

92
00:07:13,645 --> 00:07:14,437
Oh.

93
00:07:15,236 --> 00:07:16,361
Wait just a moment.

94
00:07:24,799 --> 00:07:26,387
Here, they're dry now.

95
00:07:27,208 --> 00:07:28,520
Oh, good.

96
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:30,176
Let me pour you some milk tea.

97
00:07:33,333 --> 00:07:34,864
Um, sorry.

98
00:07:35,499 --> 00:07:36,332
Could you...

99
00:07:37,566 --> 00:07:39,149
could you step out for a moment?

100
00:07:40,028 --> 00:07:40,861
Oh.

101
00:07:41,583 --> 00:07:42,500
Sure.

102
00:07:53,255 --> 00:07:55,340
Eat up. Weren't you just hungry?

103
00:07:56,285 --> 00:07:57,489
Let me tell you

104
00:07:57,514 --> 00:07:59,016
I stewed this meat for a long time.

105
00:07:59,041 --> 00:08:02,750
I put in sea buckthorn, cistanche,
and more. Here.

106
00:08:04,851 --> 00:08:06,059
Hey, eat up.

107
00:08:09,746 --> 00:08:11,590
Oh right, and this piece too.

108
00:08:12,208 --> 00:08:13,000
Here.

109
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,666
Bring your bowl over, quick.

110
00:08:24,184 --> 00:08:25,387
Dip it in this, it's good.

111
00:08:28,208 --> 00:08:29,075
Here.

112
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:29,812
How come you're not asking where I'm from?

113
00:09:30,666 --> 00:09:31,583
No need to ask.

114
00:09:32,064 --> 00:09:33,689
When you want to tell me, you will.

115
00:09:36,166 --> 00:09:38,083
Are you preparing for med school?

116
00:09:39,017 --> 00:09:40,422
It's a medical license exam.

117
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:45,666
Thank you for saving my life.

118
00:09:45,903 --> 00:09:48,278
You'll definitely become
a really good doctor.

119
00:09:49,039 --> 00:09:50,039
Saving you?

120
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:51,882
That's an exaggeration.

121
00:09:52,462 --> 00:09:53,796
At most, I just helped out.

122
00:09:55,376 --> 00:09:56,710
That was still a big help.

123
00:09:57,041 --> 00:09:59,063
Otherwise I really might have died.

124
00:10:01,008 --> 00:10:02,041
On the grasslands,

125
00:10:02,512 --> 00:10:04,399
We're all children of the Eternal Sky.

126
00:10:04,958 --> 00:10:06,625
We should help each other.

127
00:10:08,702 --> 00:10:09,702
You're right.

128
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,958
Hello, my name is Lei Zexin,
from Singapore.

129
00:10:12,958 --> 00:10:13,875
That far away!

130
00:10:13,875 --> 00:10:14,625
Yes.

131
00:10:16,375 --> 00:10:17,458
Here for sightseeing?

132
00:10:18,307 --> 00:10:19,391
Backpacking trip.

133
00:10:21,541 --> 00:10:23,125
Lei Zexin.

134
00:10:24,181 --> 00:10:25,431
Your Mandarin is quite good.

135
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:29,547
Yes, my father was from mainland China.

136
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:33,208
Then how'd you end up
in such a mess on a trip?

137
00:10:33,541 --> 00:10:34,583
And hurt too.

138
00:10:36,041 --> 00:10:37,141
I got lost.

139
00:10:38,291 --> 00:10:39,500
Looking at your wound,

140
00:10:40,041 --> 00:10:41,458
something bit you, didn't it?

141
00:10:42,541 --> 00:10:43,791
I'm embarrassed to say

142
00:10:44,853 --> 00:10:46,812
I encountered wolves on the way.

143
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:55,266
Well, you're lucky to be alive.

144
00:10:56,041 --> 00:10:57,583
Please don't make fun of me.

145
00:10:58,541 --> 00:11:00,541
Do you live here all by yourself?

146
00:11:02,458 --> 00:11:03,250
Yes.

147
00:11:04,583 --> 00:11:05,708
Just me.

148
00:11:06,508 --> 00:11:07,789
Running this guesthouse.

149
00:11:11,726 --> 00:11:13,809
What does this symbol mean?

150
00:11:14,883 --> 00:11:15,716
Amur.

151
00:11:16,575 --> 00:11:17,867
That's my name.

152
00:11:18,054 --> 00:11:20,262
You're the first patient I've treated.

153
00:11:20,287 --> 00:11:22,454
I'm leaving a signature as a memento.

154
00:11:23,031 --> 00:11:24,489
You don't mind, do you?

155
00:11:24,930 --> 00:11:25,805
Not at all.

156
00:11:26,041 --> 00:11:27,375
I think it's cute.

157
00:11:37,791 --> 00:11:40,243
Tomorrow I'll have Mongke
take you to the station.

158
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,250
It's hard to catch a ride around here.

159
00:11:42,250 --> 00:11:43,041
Station?

160
00:11:43,041 --> 00:11:43,791
Yes.

161
00:11:43,816 --> 00:11:44,733
To go where?

162
00:11:45,583 --> 00:11:47,024
Aren't you here for sightseeing?

163
00:11:47,353 --> 00:11:48,696
Nowhere you want to go?

164
00:11:51,643 --> 00:11:53,018
I don't know where to go.

165
00:11:53,833 --> 00:11:54,958
That's perfect then.

166
00:11:54,983 --> 00:11:56,274
Why don't you stay here?

167
00:11:56,723 --> 00:11:57,890
Stay here?

168
00:11:57,915 --> 00:11:58,790
Yeah.

169
00:11:58,815 --> 00:12:00,398
I'm the owner of this guesthouse.

170
00:12:00,423 --> 00:12:02,048
You can stay as long as you want.

171
00:12:02,083 --> 00:12:03,416
If you stay long enough,

172
00:12:03,416 --> 00:12:04,766
I can even give you a discount.

173
00:12:09,556 --> 00:12:10,848
This is all the cash I have.

174
00:12:11,333 --> 00:12:12,333
It's all yours.

175
00:12:13,465 --> 00:12:14,257
Wow.

176
00:12:15,088 --> 00:12:17,797
Welcome to Amur's Guesthouse!

177
00:12:17,822 --> 00:12:18,947
The grasslands are your home.

178
00:12:18,972 --> 00:12:20,739
Stay as long as you like!

179
00:12:20,785 --> 00:12:21,541
I'll hold onto this

180
00:12:21,541 --> 00:12:23,121
and refund any extra later.

181
00:12:38,041 --> 00:12:39,625
What's this dog's name?

182
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:44,166
He...

183
00:12:45,337 --> 00:12:46,308
His name is Xiaohei.

184
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:48,458
The best sheepdog on this grassland.

185
00:12:49,507 --> 00:12:50,401
Xiaohei,

186
00:12:51,861 --> 00:12:53,070
where did he go?

187
00:12:54,267 --> 00:12:55,375
He...

188
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:56,833
probably off playing somewhere.

189
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:58,562
Maybe he'll come back in a few days.

190
00:13:00,668 --> 00:13:02,418
Finally, a guest!

191
00:13:02,583 --> 00:13:03,375
Hey.

192
00:13:04,203 --> 00:13:06,041
I'll prepare your room right now.

193
00:13:06,041 --> 00:13:07,000
The best room.

194
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,916
I guarantee you'll feel right at home.

195
00:13:10,083 --> 00:13:11,083
Okay.

196
00:14:20,858 --> 00:14:21,691
You're awake.

197
00:14:24,398 --> 00:14:25,231
Come on!

198
00:14:39,416 --> 00:14:40,958
Slow down, there's more.

199
00:14:53,375 --> 00:14:54,375
Amur.

200
00:14:54,375 --> 00:14:55,041
Mm.

201
00:14:55,041 --> 00:14:56,250
This room of yours...

202
00:14:56,825 --> 00:14:58,283
is the best.

203
00:15:00,208 --> 00:15:03,101
The best room, of course,
goes to the best guest.

204
00:15:08,455 --> 00:15:10,580
Where would you like to go
these next few days?

205
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:12,125
I can be your guide.

206
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:15,333
Nowhere I want to go anymore.

207
00:15:15,358 --> 00:15:17,515
It's nice right here.

208
00:15:19,666 --> 00:15:20,875
Not going to look around?

209
00:15:21,278 --> 00:15:22,778
I'm worried you'll get bored
if you stay too long.

210
00:15:24,379 --> 00:15:25,587
Staying here

211
00:15:25,791 --> 00:15:28,015
might just be the place

212
00:15:28,429 --> 00:15:30,304
I've traveled so far to find.

213
00:15:35,161 --> 00:15:35,953
Alright.

214
00:15:36,708 --> 00:15:38,812
Stay as long as you like.

215
00:15:39,208 --> 00:15:41,000
Who told you to pay so much anyway.

216
00:15:43,187 --> 00:15:44,437
There you go again.

217
00:15:55,916 --> 00:15:56,791
Hey.

218
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:01,000
Here?

219
00:16:06,387 --> 00:16:07,460
This is the spot.

220
00:16:20,598 --> 00:16:21,556
Oh right, Amur.

221
00:16:22,291 --> 00:16:24,578
If you pass the medical license exam,

222
00:16:25,348 --> 00:16:26,681
where do you plan to work?

223
00:16:30,416 --> 00:16:31,500
A pet clinic.

224
00:16:31,525 --> 00:16:32,858
A pet clinic?

225
00:16:32,890 --> 00:16:35,600
Yes, I'm taking
the veterinary license exam.

226
00:16:36,173 --> 00:16:37,298
What?

227
00:16:38,168 --> 00:16:40,501
And you went treating me like that?

228
00:16:40,679 --> 00:16:42,671
Hey, you got better, didn't you?

229
00:16:44,554 --> 00:16:45,933
Let me tell you

230
00:16:45,958 --> 00:16:48,083
humans and animals are the same in the end.

231
00:16:48,083 --> 00:16:50,166
The medical theory is identical.

232
00:16:52,083 --> 00:16:53,666
I really can't with you.

233
00:16:53,906 --> 00:16:56,364
Actually, I should thank you instead.

234
00:16:56,708 --> 00:16:58,406
For letting me get some good practice.

235
00:16:58,625 --> 00:17:02,007
Hey, how about you become
a partner in my pet clinic?

236
00:17:03,708 --> 00:17:04,666
Partner?

237
00:17:04,691 --> 00:17:05,525
Yes.

238
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:08,875
Are you asking me to invest in you?

239
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:11,218
Hey, don't worry.

240
00:17:11,554 --> 00:17:14,429
If I'm going to rip off customers,
I won't target just one.

241
00:17:15,125 --> 00:17:16,625
You say that so righteously.

242
00:17:17,906 --> 00:17:21,039
Then how about you invest your skills
in the pet clinic?

243
00:17:25,742 --> 00:17:26,742
Speaking of which,

244
00:17:28,041 --> 00:17:29,583
what about this guesthouse?

245
00:17:29,608 --> 00:17:30,515
Will you still run it?

246
00:17:30,836 --> 00:17:31,578
And also

247
00:17:32,041 --> 00:17:33,541
your pet clinic...

248
00:17:33,958 --> 00:17:36,375
where would it be? In the city?

249
00:17:39,083 --> 00:17:40,375
The pet clinic...

250
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:43,208
Actually, it'd be more
of an animal hospital.

251
00:17:43,875 --> 00:17:44,833
Right here.

252
00:17:45,583 --> 00:17:48,750
To treat all the injured animals.

253
00:17:49,226 --> 00:17:52,208
Like when someone's horse gets hurt

254
00:17:52,208 --> 00:17:54,625
or someone's sheep rolls down a hillside

255
00:17:54,625 --> 00:17:56,083
and people's dogs...

256
00:17:56,083 --> 00:17:59,000
Auntie Wang's, Auntie Li's, and so on.

257
00:17:59,166 --> 00:18:00,416
I'll heal them all.

258
00:18:02,382 --> 00:18:03,257
Amur.

259
00:18:03,958 --> 00:18:05,458
That's a great plan.

260
00:18:05,458 --> 00:18:07,625
I'm in.

261
00:18:37,891 --> 00:18:39,391
It might leave a scar.

262
00:18:39,679 --> 00:18:41,054
If you mind,

263
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:42,579
I could get a cosmetology license too.

264
00:18:42,604 --> 00:18:44,187
Oh, please don't.

265
00:18:44,333 --> 00:18:46,333
Don't use me as your test subject, okay?

266
00:18:47,375 --> 00:18:48,750
I'm just teasing.

267
00:18:49,791 --> 00:18:52,375
Actually, a scar isn't so bad.

268
00:18:52,976 --> 00:18:54,309
It'll be a memento.

269
00:18:55,142 --> 00:18:56,809
A memento of escaping from wolves?

270
00:18:58,554 --> 00:18:59,512
A memento

271
00:19:00,570 --> 00:19:01,778
of you saving me.

272
00:19:05,947 --> 00:19:07,114
Sweet talker.

273
00:19:08,041 --> 00:19:09,041
Really.

274
00:19:09,041 --> 00:19:11,289
If I hadn't been hurt,
I wouldn't have met you.

275
00:19:13,625 --> 00:19:15,000
And I wouldn't have gotten to enjoy

276
00:19:15,424 --> 00:19:17,091
breakfast bathed in morning light.

277
00:19:19,499 --> 00:19:20,462
Then

278
00:19:21,375 --> 00:19:23,166
am I more important

279
00:19:23,191 --> 00:19:24,649
or the morning light

280
00:19:24,835 --> 00:19:26,085
or the breakfast?

281
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:27,568
You're the most important, of course.

282
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:30,078
But the morning light matters too

283
00:19:30,501 --> 00:19:32,835
and so does breakfast.

284
00:19:43,447 --> 00:19:44,697
